WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.138
The front lines in

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:05.839
eastern Ukraine,

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.440
fierce and relentless fighting

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.342
is raging in and around the city of back.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.344
Much That's where Russian forces

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.213
are now eyeing further advances

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:13.813
as they edge

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.248
towards the center of the city

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.117
from three sides.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.319
This video posted on social media

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.854
shows some of the damage left

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.722
by the ongoing battle.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:23.523
It's unclear

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.991
how many Ukrainian forces

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.393
are still inside the city.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.160
But officials say

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.295
troops are launching counterattacks

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.197
to try to preserve their access

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.366
to back from the West.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.101
Meanwhile, the US is warning

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.303
there will be real costs for China

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.572
if the country were to approve Russia

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:40.707
or provide

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.574
Russia, rather,

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.509
with lethal aid

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.778
to be used in its war on Ukraine.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:45.845
That comes after the CIA

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.881
director said the US is confident

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.683
Beijing is considering sending such aid,

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.252
but that a final decision

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.653
hasn't yet been made.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.020
The US

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.822
national security adviser weighed in.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.691
Beijing will have to make

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.492
its own decisions

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.560
about how it proceeds,

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.695
whether it provides military assistance.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.596
But if it goes down

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.064
that road,

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.433
it will come at real cost to China.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.601
And I think China's leaders are weighing

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.270
that as they make their decisions.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.005
We will watch carefully.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.473
We will be vigilant

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.441
and we will continue

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.608
to send a strong message

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.710
that we believe that sending military aid

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.045
to Russia at this time

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.114
when they are using their weapons

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.483
to bombard cities, kill civilians

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.351
and commit atrocities

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.653
would be a bad mistake.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.955
And China should want no part of it.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:29.823
So there's clear space

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:30.824
and full independence for us.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.058
Joining me here in London,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.827
it would change the entire dynamic

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.061
of this conflict, wouldn't it?

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:35.895
Yeah.
And I think that's

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.397
why you see this effort

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.932
from the US to talk about it

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.200
publicly, multiple officials

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:40.900
coming out first.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.035
We had Anthony Blinken

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.069
about ten days ago.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.071
He, according to State Sullivan, laid out

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.506
those potential consequences

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.775
in his meeting with Chinese top diplomat

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:49.242
Wang Yi.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:49.876
We don't know what

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:50.710
those consequences are.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.778
I think it's safe to assume

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.612
there would be economic

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.746
consequences, sanctions

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.447
and things like that.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.181
And the US

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.683
clearly making the point

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.051
that this would be a red line.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.085
I think they hope that

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.320
this will be a deterrent,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.621
that they won't have to get to the point

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.490
of enforcing those consequences.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.591
And, you know,

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.258
we have to be really clear

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.092
about what they're saying here

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.160
because the CIA director

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:07.660
was out

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.996
on Sunday as well on CBS

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:10.530
and he said, look,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.998
we're confident in his words

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.333
that the Chinese leadership

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.901
is considering the provision

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.702
of lethal equipment.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.903
They don't know that they have concrete

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:17.337
plans.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.805
There certainly hasn't been a decision.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.073
There hasn't been any shipment,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.374
he said, as of yet.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.442
But they are confident

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.343
they are considering it.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:23.776
So they're trying

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.644
to get out ahead of this.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.211
And obviously,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.546
if the China does make the decision

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.647
it would come at a time

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.082
when the US believes

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.050
that Russia has overestimated

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.318
its ability on the battlefield.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:32.986
Take a listen to a little

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.087
bit more of Bill Burns

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.957
I think Putin is

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.425
right now entirely too

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.095
confident of his ability to wear down

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.731
Ukraine to grind away.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:45.131
And that's

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.866
what he's giving every evidence

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.935
that he's determined to do right now.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.303
At some point,

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.804
he's going to have to face up

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.972
to increasing costs

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:53.740
as well

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.141
in coffins coming home

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.210
to some of the poorest parts of Russia.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:57.677
There's a

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.913
cumulative economic damage

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.581
to Russia as well.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.283
Huge reputational damage.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.384
It's not exactly been

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.552
a great advertise ban

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.053
for Russian arms sales.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.821
So this is going to build over time.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.956
But right now,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:10.823
the honest answer,

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:14.527
I think Putin is quite determined,

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.828
quite determined and Bill Burns,

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.864
Max, also pointed out that Russia's

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:18.464
military ties

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.133
with Iran are, in his words,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.268
moving at a pretty fast clip.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:22.769
So clearly

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.404
they're trying to avoid the same thing

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:25.171
happening with China.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.206
Because that could

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.373
turn the tide on the battlefield

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.008
and be a very dangerous situation

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.376
for Ukraine. How much?

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.812
I guess it depends

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.080
what sort of weapons they receive.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.981
But, you know,

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.082
we keep hearing these reports

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.550
say running out of

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.618
different times of weaponry

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.320
and the soldiers are exhausted

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.821
and so many are dying.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.488
How much difference

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.290
would that support from China make?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.091
Do you think?

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.160
I think it would make a major difference.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.795
China has a major weapons

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.529
industry of its own.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.030
The intelligence that

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:51.664
Washington colleagues

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:52.565
have reported on before

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.901
this is that it was ammunition and drones

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.936
that China was considering sending,

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.538
not sort of large scale artillery

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.239
and things like that.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.039
But that is

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.541
really the front end of the issue

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.141
at the moment

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.676
because of the type of fighting

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.777
that we're seeing in the Donbass,

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.912
really heavy

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.314
expenditure of of of ammunition.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.282
Drones are heavily

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.817
and we've seen them overnight

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.319
attacking in particular the Kiev region.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.621
Ukraine has shut down most of them.

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:16.656
But these are the sort of more disposable

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.790
elements of weaponry

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.058
that Russia is burning through

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.793
at an incredibly fast rate.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.328
It's really sort of reset

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.696
the expectations of the military

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:24.530
industrial complex

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.865
on the side of Ukraine

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.467
in terms of the transatlantic alliance.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.535
And we know that that Russia

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:30.803
has been looking to Iran

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.572
and are now looking potentially

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.540
at China Clare, thank you.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.708
Overnight, Ukrainian forces

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:36.809
shot down 11

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:37.477
Russian attack

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:39.812
drones, including nine in the airspace

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.780
around Kiev.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.348
At least two people have been killed

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.149
and four others

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.550
injured in a drone attack.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.752
And Chmielewski,

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.986
a city as about 200 miles

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.421
southwest of Kiev.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.555
These attacks are coming.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:50.790
As President Zelensky said

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.457
in recent days,

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.892
he does still believe

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.194
Ukraine can win the war this year

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.496
as long as its allies

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.898
remain united and continue in delivering

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.199
weapons to Ukraine.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.100
CNN's Jim

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.835
Acosta is live in eastern Ukraine.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.370
On the ground tracking these attacks.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.139
Alex, what are we seeing that's happening

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:07.240
overnight and on the ground

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:10.810
Well, good morning, Kaitlan.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.679
While these 14 drones were these

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:13.346
Iranian made

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.314
kamikaze drones

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.115
that were flown at two different cities

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:16.916
in Ukraine overnight,

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.484
come on, jetski, which you mentioned,

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:19.085
that's where at least

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.186
two people died

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:22.889
in a so-called double tap attack.

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.390
They were first responders

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.526
responding to another drone strike

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.126
when they were killed.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.695
Three others were injured.

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:29.829
11 of these drones

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.230
were fired, active,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:31.998
at least nine of them

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:34.100
shot down by air defenses.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.535
But these sirens wailed

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.470
for some five and a half hours

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.073
because this was a multi wave attack.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.574
That is not normal.

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.375
Normally, these sirens

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.743
go for a couple of minutes,

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:44.310
then are turned off.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.244
And it really speaks to the fact

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.245
that in cities like this

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.080
where people are living

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.481
relatively normal, lives,

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:49.882
they live under constant

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:50.950
fear of these attacks.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.352
And it really does highlight

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:54.087
the major security concerns

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:55.588
around President Biden's trip

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.390
to Kiev last Monday.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.359
Yeah,
and of course, the fact that those are

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:00.026
the Iranian made

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:00.626
drones comes

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:01.861
as we're having the broader discussion

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.262
about maybe China potentially

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:04.864
providing weapons to Russia.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:05.598
Also, Alex, you know,

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.367
we're hearing from Republican lawmakers

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:07.900
who are being

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.435
very critical of the White House

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.470
because they have not sent

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.872
the F-16 fighter jets to Ukraine.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:13.573
President Biden

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:15.475
actually weighed in on this to ABC News.

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:16.743
And this is what he said about the

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.777
idea of sending them

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:20.313
president.

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:20.680
So Wolinsky

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.882
continues to say what he really needs

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.450
are F-16s.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.085
Will you send F-16s?

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:26.819
Look,

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.122
we're sending him

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:30.790
what our

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.092
seasoned military thinks he needs now.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.861
He needs tanks,

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:35.928
he needs artillery,

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:36.963
he needs air defense

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.031
including another high marks.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.900
There are things he needs now.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.335
You don't think he needs F-16s now?

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:44.670
No, he doesn't need F-16s now.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.105
Alex, that's just something that

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:48.541
Ukrainian officials flatly disagree with.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.912
This is kind of like the debate over

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.280
tanks, Caitlin, where the U.S.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:54.747
said that

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:55.882
that Ukraine doesn't

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:56.916
need em on Abrams tanks,

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:57.884
but they decided to give them

00:06:57.884 --> 00:06:58.885
to Ukraine in the end

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.453
so that the Germans would release

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.655
those those leopard to tanks. The U.S.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:03.956
standing firmly

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.491
behind that line of President Biden

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.193
that right now in this fight,

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:09.395
Ukraine does not need fighter jets

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:10.930
that right now

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.399
the priority should be on artillery,

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:16.502
on longer range rockets, on tanks.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.071
That fighter jets are not necessary

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:19.505
for this fight.

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:21.307
They're not ideologically opposed

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:22.341
to sending fighter jets.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.109
In fact,

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:24.510
I've been told that they wouldn't

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.611
it wouldn't bother them

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:26.679
if other countries

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:27.513
sent their fighter jets.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:28.381
But right now, the U.S.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:31.517
priority is on the ground fighting.

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.419
That is a priority, getting them stuff

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:34.487
very quickly.

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.621
And we are starting

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:36.889
to see those shipments

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:37.924
coming in

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:39.559
a major sticking point right

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:41.227
now is over the attack arms.

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:41.861
Kaitlin is you know,

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:43.863
those are the longer range rockets

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:44.297
that fly

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:47.066
some 200 miles or 300 kilometers.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.167
Ukrainian saying

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.268
they need those right now

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:51.304
to hit Russian targets, to hit

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:53.005
command post, to hit

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:55.107
ammunitions depots, supply lines,

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.509
targets in Crimea.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:57.176
The U.S.

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:59.011
has only sent rockets

00:07:59.011 --> 00:07:59.846
that go

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:02.949
as far as 100 miles or 150 kilometers

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:06.018
because there is a real American fear

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.787
about provocation,

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:08.855
about the fact

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:09.722
that Russia would see

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:10.990
those longer range rockets

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.625
as an escalation.

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:14.293
Now, Ukraine, of course, disagrees.

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:15.328
So that is a major

00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.762
sticking point between the U.S.

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:17.964
and Ukraine.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.298
Certainly a point of contention.

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:20.433
Alex Marquardt, thank you.

